cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this design, the evaluation protocol or the dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Embodied GUI Agent: a physical robotic arm with force-vision feedback for real-device mobile GUI automation"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/xiaowangkkk1231/embodied-gui-agent/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xiaowangkkk1231/embodied-gui-agent"
url: "https://github.com/xiaowangkkk1231/embodied-gui-agent"
abstract: >-
  Design and evaluation protocol for an embodied GUI agent that operates a real smartphone
  through an XY robotic gantry with a conductive stylus, assisted by a Bluetooth/USB HID
  channel. The repository documents the hardware BOM, calibration pipeline (homography, tool
  offset, visual servoing), the HID/robot arbitration policy, a force-based tap-acceptance
  classifier, and a 60-task benchmark with five control groups.
keywords:
  - GUI agent
  - embodied agent
  - mobile automation
  - robotic UI testing
  - hardware-in-the-loop
  - force feedback
  - Android input
